OL,2,V55555555CFIRE GUTS 'FREE
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CMANDELA' OFFICES
OL,4,B
OL,5, Fire gutted the offices of a group
OL,6, campaigning for the release of black
OL,7, South African leader Nelson Mandela.
OL,9, And one of the group's officers was
OL,10, later arrested on unspecified charges.
OL,12, The arrested man is Mr Aubrey Mokoena,
OL,13, publicity secretary of the Release
OL,14, Mandela Campaign in Johannesburg.
OL,16, He had accused police of ransacking
OL,17, office files and starting the fire.
OL,18,B
OL,19, A civil rights lawyer said Mr Mokoena
OL,20, was being charged under the Prisons Act
OL,21, which covers a wide range of offences.
OL,23,F]DFrom 06-03-96 / teletextarchive.com
