PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772832103
OL,1,Q{$~k4oz%h7}h7q#################G21/44
OL,2,Q/.!+.!/*%/*%/"-' C  MARSH IN EURO    Qj
OL,3,Q5GISLE OF MAN      CTITLE DEFENCE    Qj
OL,4,Q#######################################
OL,5,FBasildon firemanCTerry MarshFwill
OL,6,Fdefend his European light-welterweight
OL,7,Ftitle against DaneCMohamed KowoyaFat
OL,8,FPalace Lido, Isle of Man, on April 12.
OL,10,FMeanwhile, Marsh has been offered a
OL,11,Ffight with WBC champion Lonnie Smith.
OL,13,FBut he would rather wait to meet the
OL,14,Fwinner of next week's WBA title fight
OL,15,Fbetween Patricio Oliva, of Italy, and
OL,16,FUbaldo Sacco in Monte Carlo.
OL,18,FThe delayed British heavyweight title
OL,19,Fcontest between holderCHughroy Currie
OL,20,FandCHorace NoticeFwill be a supporting
OL,21,Fbout on the Marsh-Kowoya bill.
OL,22,                    C  Bruno poser >>>>>
OL,23,Q]GFrom 06-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49622
SC,0022
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772832103
OL,1,Q{$~k4oz%h7}h7q#################G22/44
OL,2,Q/.!+.!/*%/*%/"-'   C  EBU POSER      Qj
OL,3,Q5GEUROPEAN TITLE     CFOR BRUNO      Qj
OL,4,Q#######################################
OL,5,FFrank Bruno must soon decide whether to
OL,6,Fkeep his European heavyweight crown.
OL,8,FBruno, who bludgeoned the EBU title
OL,9,Ffrom Swede Anders Eklund last year, has
OL,10,Fbeen ordered to defend it against
OL,11,FDutchman Andre Van Den Oetelaar.
OL,13,FPurse offers are due shortly, but the
OL,14,FLondoner, now aiming for the world
OL,15,Ftitle, is likely to find that fight
OL,16,Fdifficult to fit into his plans.
OL,18,FManager Terry Lawless said it was
OL,19,Fsomething he and Bruno must discuss.
OL,21,FBut Lawless added: "He does not want to
OL,22,Fgive anything up "C   Marsh defence >>>
OL,23,Q]GFrom 06-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49623
SC,0023
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772832103
OL,1,Qk7jwh7}h7}j5~s"##################G23/44
OL,2,Q*%*-*%/*%/*%,'   C     USA WOMEN'S Q  j
OL,3,Q5GPrinceton, N Jersey CINDOOR CH'SHIPQj
OL,4,Q#######################################
OL,5,FMartina Navratilova took another step
OL,6,Fon the way to her expected place in
OL,7,Fthe final with an easy 6-0 6-4 second
OL,8,Fround win over Czech Andrea Holikova.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FTwo Czechs who won were Helena Sukova,
OL,11,Fwho beat Elise Burgin 6-1 6-2, and Hana
OL,12,FMandlikova, a 6-3 6-2 victor against
OL,13,FSylvia Hanika.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FBut seventh seed Barbara Potter went
OL,16,Fout 6-3 2-6 6-3 to Alycia Moulton who
OL,17,Fhad returned to action after a couple
OL,18,Fof days in bed with flu.
OL,20,FNinth seed Anne White also fell by the
OL,21,Fwayside after being beaten 6-3 6-2 by
OL,22,Fanother American, Terry Phelps.
OL,23,Q]GFrom 06-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
