PN,49625
SC,0025
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772832103
OL,1,Q~+${$h7-ju?jw"!###############G25/44
OL,2,Q+.!/*%/"-'*%/*- /C  MOVES TO EASE    Qj
OL,3,Q5GTCCB MEETING    C BOUNCER PROBLEM  Qj
OL,4,Q#######################################
OL,5,FThe TCCB has made the first moves to
OL,6,Fease the umpire's interpretation of
OL,7,Fshort-pitched bowling.
OL,9,FThe Board has formulated a new wording
OL,10,Fof the law covering bouncers and it
OL,11,Fwill be passed onto the ICC for debate
OL,12,Fat their annual meeting in July.
OL,14,FMeanwhile, a call for uncovered pitches
OL,15,Fin the County Ch'ship has been rejected
OL,17,FA shoot-out in one-day matches will be
OL,18,Fbrought in next season with five
OL,19,Fplayers on each side bowling at a set
OL,20,Fof stumps when games are hit by rain.
OL,22,FFred Titmus is to succeed Alec Bedser
OL,23,Fon England's selection panel.C
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49626
SC,0026
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772832103
OL,1,Q{$j5~c1{$z5##################G26/44
OL,2,Q/*%+.!+.!/.!,.!     Wj5~k4h7}h7}   Qj
OL,3,Q5CPERKINS QUITS     W+.!/*%/"-'*%/   Qj
OL,4,Q#######################################
OL,5,FWales second row forward John Perkins
OL,6,Fhas made a shock decision to quit the
OL,7,Finternational scene.
OL,9,FThe Pontypool skipper said he had four
OL,10,Fgreat years at the top.
OL,12,FPerkins, 32, added: "I feel the Welsh
OL,13,Fselectors, with their eyes on the World
OL,14,FCup, should look to younger players."
OL,16,FBut the lock, with nearly 500 games
OL,17,Fbehind him for Pontypool, stressed he
OL,18,Fwould continue to play club rugby for
OL,19,Fanother two years.
OL,21,FPerkins had the unusual distinction of
OL,22,Fwinning his 18 caps without a break.
OL,23,Q]GFrom 06-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
